# The mirror of steer-left.inputs: a single constant turn, held right.
#
# See steer-left.inputs for why the pair exists and how to capture it. The two
# are only useful together - a fitted steering constant that reproduces one
# direction and not the other is describing an asymmetry that is not in the
# input, so the pair is what
# `crates/trace/tests/yaw_authority_ground_truth.rs` checks.
#
#     just trace --port 47810 --script verification/scenarios/steer-right.inputs \
#         --script-lead 2 --warmup-hold cross --warmup 6 \
#         --out data/traces/talons-junction-steer-right.csv

200 cross right
